    "text": "In a Coolidge tube, the potential difference used to accelerate the electron is increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kV</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>49</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kV</mi></math>. As a result, the difference between the wavelength of <em>K</em><sub>α</sub>-line and minimum wavelength becomes two times. Then the wavelength of <em>K</em><sub>α</sub>-line is<br /><br />\r<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi><mi>c</mi></mrow><mi>e</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>∘</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>",
